{"id":"ee11792e-6dc8-4390-abf7-a8b1fd62590c","revision":0,"last_node_id":22,"last_link_id":28,"nodes":[{"id":1,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[0,-400],"size":[2900,340],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Arbor · Edit by scene — pictures × instructions as one tree (Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo edit)\n\nThe pictures are a tree (**Load Folder**: one named branch per scene, from *arbor_qwen_storyboard*), and so are the edits (**Panel**: `# scene` + one edit per line). Each scene gets **its own** edits — two for *Arrival*, one for *The village*, two for *Festival* — and every shot of a scene gets all of them.\n\n1. **Cross Reference** pairs the two trees branch by branch: every shot becomes a sub-branch `{scene;shot}` holding the picture once per edit (*A*), next to those edits (*B*). Uneven counts are fine — that is what branches are for.\n2. **XY Lists** in *zip* mode takes both trees — pictures on *x*, instructions on *y* — and flattens them side by side: item k of one with item k of the other, so the edit model runs once per (shot, edit). Its *shape* keeps the pictures' branches for putting the results back.\n3. **Construct Tree** puts the results back into `{scene;shot}`; **List Item** `0` takes the untouched picture of every shot, and **Merge** appends the edits to it on the same path → each row of the **Image Grid** is *original, edit 1, edit 2…*, labelled `Arrival · 1`.\n4. **Save by Path** keeps the structure on disk: `output/arbor/edits/0-0 · Arrival · 1/…`.\n\nRun *arbor_qwen_storyboard* first (or point Load Folder at any folder of folders). Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo edits best with concrete, local instructions — add, remove or recolor something — rather than restyling the whole picture."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## Arbor · Edit by scene — pictures × instructions as one tree (Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo edit)\n\nThe pictures are a tree (**Load Folder**: one named branch per scene, from *arbor_qwen_storyboard*), and so are the edits (**Panel**: `# scene` + one edit per line). Each scene gets **its own** edits — two for *Arrival*, one for *The village*, two for *Festival* — and every shot of a scene gets all of them.\n\n1. **Cross Reference** pairs the two trees branch by branch: every shot becomes a sub-branch `{scene;shot}` holding the picture once per edit (*A*), next to those edits (*B*). Uneven counts are fine — that is what branches are for.\n2. **XY Lists** in *zip* mode takes both trees — pictures on *x*, instructions on *y* — and flattens them side by side: item k of one with item k of the other, so the edit model runs once per (shot, edit). Its *shape* keeps the pictures' branches for putting the results back.\n3. **Construct Tree** puts the results back into `{scene;shot}`; **List Item** `0` takes the untouched picture of every shot, and **Merge** appends the edits to it on the same path → each row of the **Image Grid** is *original, edit 1, edit 2…*, labelled `Arrival · 1`.\n4. **Save by Path** keeps the structure on disk: `output/arbor/edits/0-0 · Arrival · 1/…`.\n\nRun *arbor_qwen_storyboard* first (or point Load Folder at any folder of folders). Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo edits best with concrete, local instructions — add, remove or recolor something — rather than restyling the whole picture."},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":2,"type":"Arbor_LoadFolder","pos":[0,0],"size":[420,238],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"文件夹","name":"folder","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"folder"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"类型","name":"kind","type":"COMFY_DYNAMICCOMBO_V3","widget":{"name":"kind"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"文件匹配","name":"kind.pattern","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"kind.pattern"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"子文件夹","name":"subfolders","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"subfolders"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"排序","name":"sort","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"sort"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"数量上限","name":"limit","type":